 {"q": "What does the end of Acts suggest Luke most wanted to show?", "options": ["How Paul's trial ended", "That the message reached the capital of the world and was preached there 'without hindrance'", "That Paul abandoned the Jews entirely", "That Rome had become Christian"], "answer": 1, "why": "Luke ends with Paul preaching unhindered in Rome, the 'ends of the earth' of Acts 1:8, and leaves the trial untold."},
